    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7nzmZD",
      "title": "Add Swell L1 ownership-transfer task (055)",
      "author": "sbvegan",
      "number": 1476,
      "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds task `055-swell-l1-ownership-transfers`, which transfers **L1 ownership of the Swell chain (chainId 1923)** from the standard OP Mainnet L1PAO Safe (`0x5a0Aae59D09fccBdDb6C6CcEB07B7279367C3d2A`) to AltLayer's new owner Safe (`0xa83F1334c6a8Daca576Dc14020d9d2b1b16a8Dfa`). Swell is winding down and AltLayer is taking over to finish the wind-down.\r\n\r\nContracts moved via the `TransferOwners` template:\r\n- **ProxyAdmin** (`0x4C4710a4Ec3F514A492CC6460818C4A6A6269dd6`) — `transferOwnership`\r\n- **DisputeGameFactoryProxy** (`0x87690676786cDc8cCA75A472e483AF7C8F2f0F57`) — `transferOwnership`\r\n\r\nThe chain's DelayedWETH is v1.5.0 (post-U16) and not ownable, so the template skips it at build time. Swell has been removed from the public superchain-registry (ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry#1247); its addresses are loaded via `fallbackAddressesJsonPath` from `addresses.json` (verified with `op-fetcher`) and it reuses OP Mainnet's standard SuperchainConfig.\r\n\r\n## Status\r\n\r\n⚠️ **`DRAFT, NOT READY TO SIGN`** — requires Optimism Governance approval before signing. Domain/message hashes in `VALIDATION.md` were generated at task creation (2026-06-15) with pinned Safe nonces; live nonces must be re-verified and the task re-simulated before signing.\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-06-18T06:28:45Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 236,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7nqEc4",
      "title": "Add SystemConfigGasLimit template (gas-limit-only)",
      "author": "sbvegan",
      "number": 1474,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **`src/template/SystemConfigGasLimit.sol`** — a minimal `L2TaskBase` template that calls only `SystemConfig.setGasLimit` (no EIP-1559 params). It's the gas-limit-only counterpart to the existing `SystemConfigGasParams`.\n\n## Why\n\nRe-issuing `setGasLimit` re-emits the gas `ConfigUpdate` without touching EIP-1559 params — useful whenever only the gas limit needs to change. The immediate motivation is the **Karst (U19) gas-limit reset**, where re-emitting the `ConfigUpdate` (to clear the post-activation +55 MGas op-node/kona bug) is the *entire* mitigation; the EIP-1559 params are unrelated.\n\n## Details\n\n- Reads `gasParams.gasLimit` from `config.toml` and applies it to each chain in `l2chains`.\n- Validates `SystemConfig.gasLimit()` post-execution.\n- The gas limit is authorized by the SystemConfig owner, so `safeAddressString` defaults to `\"SystemConfigOwner\"` (resolved per-chain from `SystemConfig.owner()`); override in `config.toml` if a different root safe is required.\n- Does not modify the shared `SystemConfigGasParams` template — fully additive.\n\n## Status / follow-ups\n\nSplit out from the U19 gas-reset tasks PR (#1470) so the template can be reviewed independently. No example task / unit test is included yet — happy to add one mirroring `test/tasks/example/eth/006-system-config-gas-params` + the `SystemConfigGasParams` entries in `TaskManager.t.sol` / `Regression.t.sol` if desired before merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-06-17T20:25:13Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-06-18T22:12:07Z",
      "additions": 118,
      "deletions": 0
    }
